 Browse GitHub issues across repositories using an account connected in Settings → Integrations.
 Use `viewer` with an empty request object to verify the account identity. List, detail and comments read as the explicitly selected account. The current directory does not restrict the personal queue.
 
 ```bash
 keryx issues list --login LOGIN --request '{"source":"assigned","state":"open"}' --json
 ```
 
 Use `assigned`, `created`, `mentioned` or `subscribed` for the source. Pass an opaque `nextCursor` as `cursor` on the next call with the same account and filters. Use the returned issue `ref` in a `detail` or `comments` request. `project` reads a selected GitHub Project by owner and number or node ID. `move` explicitly updates the selected item’s Status after checking its current value and rereads it. Project reads and writes require matching Projects permissions.
 
 Use `origin` to resolve an existing Flow or session’s issue as the selected viewer. Use `workspace` to inspect an issue’s local checkout, session and Flow. `open-session` and `prepare-flow` resume or create the linked work in the matching checkout. A failed access check means the selected account or its permissions need attention. Reconnect the account and refresh. If the Desktop reports an incompatible CLI, choose the bundled Keryx CLI in Settings.
 
 ## review
 
 The Desktop Review board reads the current project’s GitHub pull requests with
 `keryx review board --json`. Select a connected remote using `--repo owner/name`,
 filter history with `--state open|closed|merged|all`, or read one pull request’s
 discussion and checks with `--number N`. A partial list includes warnings.
 `keryx review board --json --repositories` lists the configured GitHub.com fetch
 remotes without contacting GitHub, with the origin repository first.
 
+`keryx review reviews --json [--repo owner/name]` lists the selected account's local
+Reviews of a connected repository: one per pull request, newest activity first. Each
+Review carries its pull request card, its state (`queued`, `running`, `needs_answer`,
+`stopped`, `ready`, `published` or `closed`), its freshness (`current`, or `behind` with
+the number of new commits, `null` when unknown, and whether the branch was rewritten),
+its rounds newest first with their attempts, the findings of the latest reviewed round,
+the publication outcome, the source, the linked Flow and the total tokens. Reports and
+reviewer sessions are not included. Archived and deleted attempts are left out. Commit
+counts are read for up to 25 Reviews per call; the rest, and any comparison GitHub
+refuses, show an unknown count and a warning. Without a local review store the list is
+empty and no store is created.
+
 `keryx review accounts list --json` lists local GitHub CLI accounts and their status.
 `keryx review accounts project --json` shows the current project's selection.
 Use `keryx review accounts bind --login LOGIN --json` to verify and select an account
 for the project and its linked worktrees. Add `--repo owner/name` to check a connected
 remote other than the default. The board, private review fetch and local watcher
 use the selected account. The credentials stay in GitHub CLI.
 Use `keryx review accounts bind --skip --json` to continue without a connection.
 Changing or removing a connection pauses the project's watchers. Enable the
 watcher manually after choosing an account.
 
 `keryx review desk-run start --json --repo owner/name --repository-id ID --viewer LOGIN --number N --base SHA --head SHA`
 requests review of a card’s displayed revision. With the same repository, viewer and PR flags, use
 `status` to read progress and history, or `cancel --id UUID` to stop a specific attempt.
 Manual reviews start without a token limit. For scheduled reviews, omit `budgetTokens` or set it to `null` for unlimited tokens. A positive integer sets the per-run cap, including values above 250,000. Saved rules retain their explicit limits. The time limit is configured independently.
 
 Load a deferred report with `status --id UUID`. A retry creates a fresh attempt after an interrupted review. Keryx stores results locally. A later review can send excerpts from earlier reports and linked Flow evidence to the configured model provider as context.
 
 `keryx review desk-publish --json --repo owner/name --repository-id ID --viewer LOGIN --number N --request <JSON>`
 prepares the publication form for a local review attempt. Use `kind: preview` with
 the attempt UUID to read the draft, or `kind: save` with settings to keep the draft

